 only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Hawaii is among the most Democratic states in presidential politics, having backed the Democratic nominee in every election since 1984. Recent results have been decisive, with margins generally exceeding twenty points, and the state's partisan lean points the same direction. No candidate-specific polling or expert ratings are available for this open-seat contest, so the outlook rests on these fundamentals.\n\nThe national climate offers some additional comfort for Democrats, with surveys showing voters favoring a congressional check on the president and trusting the party more on key issues. Even in cycles where Republicans performed well nationally, Hawaii's margin has stayed well into double digits. The Republican path here would require a political realignment far larger than anything in recent precedent.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9253, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8734, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8703, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9295, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.874, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8784, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.877, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.874, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8862, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.878, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8719, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8743, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.8792, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.8767, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.879, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.8843, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.8748, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.8714, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0